/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  batch19_feed_switch_purge / system/controlDict

  Time control for the A5 load-then-purge cycle on the batch13 bed.  The
  load step is batch13's (stoichiometric front at t_st = 3040.5 s, printed
  pre-run); the switch fires at 3600 s (recipe, flowsheetDict) and the
  purge runs to 9000 s -- long enough for the desorption tail to hand a
  visible fraction of the loading back, short of full regeneration (the
  favourable isotherm makes desorption slow; that asymmetry IS the
  lesson).

  timeStepping adaptive: the stiff Rosenbrock23, exactly as batch13.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoBatch;
description   "A5 feed switch: CO2/He load to 3600 s (batch13 anchors), then pure-He purge to 9000 s -- amended feed commitment ledgered, frozen breakthrough KPIs, desorption duty as the same state difference";

verbosity     3;

// ---- Time integration ----
startTime       0;        // s
endTime         9000;     // s   (3600 load + 5400 purge)
deltaT          0.05;     // s   (only relevant in timeStepping fixed)
writeInterval   300;      // s   (trajectory row + <t>/bed.profile)
timeStepping    adaptive; // Rosenbrock23
